.SS "Minor Changes"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Add experimental support for the \fRView Transitions API\fP via \fRdocument\&.startViewTransition\fP to enable CSS animated transitions on SPA navigations in your application\&. (\fR#10916\fP)

.PP
The simplest approach to enabling a View Transition in your React Router app is via the new \fR<Link unstable_viewTransition>\fP prop\&. This will cause the navigation DOM update to be wrapped in \fRdocument\&.startViewTransition\fP which will enable transitions for the DOM update\&. Without any additional CSS styles, you'll get a basic cross-fade animation for your page\&.

.PP
If you need to apply more fine-grained styles for your animations, you can leverage the \fRunstable_useViewTransitionState\fP hook which will tell you when a transition is in progress and you can use that to apply classes or styles:

.PP
.PP
.nf
function ImageLink(to, src, alt) {
  let isTransitioning = unstable_useViewTransitionState(to);
  return (
    <Link to={to} unstable_viewTransition>
      <img
        src={src}
        alt={alt}
        style={{
          viewTransitionName: isTransitioning ? "image\-expand" : "",
        }}
      />
    </Link>
  );
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
You can also use the \fR<NavLink unstable_viewTransition>\fP shorthand which will manage the hook usage for you and automatically add a \fRtransitioning\fP class to the \fR<a>\fP during the transition:

.PP
.PP
.nf
a\&.transitioning img {
  view\-transition\-name: "image\-expand";
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
<NavLink to={to} unstable_viewTransition>
  <img src={src} alt={alt} />
</NavLink>
.fi
.PP

.PP
For an example usage of View Transitions with React Router, check out \fRour fork\fP of the \fRAstro Records\fP demo\&.

.PP
For more information on using the View Transitions API, please refer to the \fRSmooth and simple transitions with the View Transitions API\fP guide from the Google Chrome team\&.

.PP
Please note, that because the \fRViewTransition\fP API is a DOM API, we now export a specific \fRRouterProvider\fP from \fRreact-router-dom\fP with this functionality\&. If you are importing \fRRouterProvider\fP from \fRreact-router\fP, then it will not support view transitions\&. (\fR#10928\fP
.PP
