.PP
.SH "6\&.4\&.0"
.PP
Whoa this is a big one! \fR6\&.4\&.0\fP brings all the data loading and mutation APIs over from Remix\&. Here's a quick high level overview, but it's recommended you go check out the \fRdocs\fP, especially the \fRfeature overview\fP and the \fRtutorial\fP\&.

.PP
\fBNew APIs\fP

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Create your router with \fRcreateMemoryRouter\fP/\fRcreateBrowserRouter\fP/\fRcreateHashRouter\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Render your router with \fR<RouterProvider>\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Load data with a Route \fRloader\fP and mutate with a Route \fRaction\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Handle errors with Route \fRerrorElement\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Submit data with the new \fR<Form>\fP component
.IP "\(bu" 2
Perform in-page data loads and mutations with \fRuseFetcher()\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Defer non-critical data with \fRdefer\fP and \fRAwait\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Manage scroll position with \fR<ScrollRestoration>\fP
.PP

.PP
\fBNew Features\fP

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Perform path-relative navigations with \fR<Link relative="path">\fP (#9160)
.PP

.PP
\fBBug Fixes\fP

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Path resolution is now trailing slash agnostic (#8861)
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRuseLocation\fP returns the scoped location inside a \fR<Routes location>\fP component (#9094)
.IP "\(bu" 2
respect the \fR<Link replace>\fP prop if it is defined (#8779)
.PP

.PP
\fBUpdated Dependencies\fP

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRreact-router@6\&.4\&.0\fP 
.PP

